README = 'develop.uganda V235 — UGANDA LUT MIXER PRO\n\nPURPOSE\nV235 turns the existing Uganda Scene LUT system into a practical on-camera\ncolor mixer without replacing the proven CameraX recording pipeline.\n\nWHAT IS NEW\n1. Six plain-language controls are present on EVERY LUT:\n   01 GREEN  — salad, leaves, vegetation\n   02 RED    — meat, signs, clothes\n   03 YELLOW — banana, sun, warm lights\n   04 BLUE   — sky, water, cool glass\n   05 ORANGE — food, brick, warm light\n   06 BROWN  — earth, wood, coffee\n\n2. Each control runs 0–200%.\n   100% = the designed LUT exactly.\n   Below 100% gently reduces that color family.\n   Above 100% increases that color family.\n   Values auto-save independently per LUT and per camera scope.\n\n3. The authored V231/V232 five-color Scene Palette remains available.\n   V235 does not throw away the earlier work; it adds the simple six-color\n   layer after it.\n\n4. HOLD ORIGINAL remains available for instant comparison.\n\n5. V234 navy-safe UI principles are included in V235:\n   dark navy sheet, thin accent borders, bottom placement and scroll-safe lists.\n\nSAFETY / MASTER POLICY\nThe original CameraX MP4 remains untouched.\nThe live screen grade is an operator preview.\nCOLOR_MASTER.mp4 is the separate final render using Media3 SingleColorLut 17^3,\nthe authored scene palette, the six-color V235 mixer, and H.264/AAC re-encode.\n\nVERSION\nversionCode 23500\nversionName 235.0-uganda-lut-mixer-pro\n'
(ROOT / "README-V235-UGANDA-LUT-MIXER-PRO.txt").write_text(README, encoding="utf-8")

